# Copy this file to docker/.env and adjust before running
# `docker compose up --build -d` from the docker/ directory.
# See documentation/DOCKER_DEPLOYMENT.md for the full walkthrough.

# ---- Which model the llm-engine container loads ----
# Only one model runs at a time (VRAM constraint - same rule as the
# bare-metal local-llm/config.yaml). Pick one of the two preset pairs below
# by uncommenting it, or point LLM_MODEL_FILE at a different GGUF you've
# downloaded into docker/models/.

# Phi-4-mini-instruct (recommended default - ~2.5GB, lower VRAM, faster;
# used as the "fast_default" role for batch briefings on the bare-metal path)
LLM_MODEL_FILE=phi-4-mini-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf
LLM_MODEL_NAME=phi-4-mini-instruct-q4_k_m

# Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct (the "specialist" model - ~4.7GB, better
# structured Cisco IOS-XE syntax handling, needs more VRAM). To switch:
# comment out the Phi-4-mini pair above and uncomment these two instead.
# LLM_MODEL_FILE=qwen2.5-coder-7b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf
# LLM_MODEL_NAME=qwen2.5-coder-7b-instruct-q4_k_m

# ---- llama-server tuning (see local-llm/README.md's "Memory safety"
# section for why these specific defaults matter - they're the fix for a
# real RAM-growth issue found and fixed on the bare-metal path; keep them
# unless you have a specific reason to change them) ----
LLM_CTX_SIZE=2048
LLM_NGL=99
LLM_PARALLEL=1
LLM_CACHE_RAM=0

# ---- Webapp ----
# Host port the web UI is reachable on (http://<server-ip>:<this>).
WEBAPP_PORT=8000
